[{"_1":2},"llms/mdx",{"_3":4},"data","# Data model (/docs/platform/administration/access-control/data-model)\n\n\n\nThe `connectors/authz/pki.json` schema defines the entities in the `pki` authorization namespace. A policy identifies a resource type through `namespace: pki`, `schema_name` and `entity_type`. For example, `ca.certificate` identifies the `certificate` entity type in the `ca` schema.\n\nSchema relationships [#schema-relationships]\n\nEach arrow starts at the entity that declares the relationship and points to its `target_entity`. The value of `foreign_key`, the source column, appears below the label. In `pki.json`, each relationship's `name` matches that column. Select the diagram to enlarge it and scroll through it.\n\n<Mermaid\n  chart=\"flowchart TB\n    accTitle: Relationships in the pki.json schema\n    accDescr: Nine relationships declared in pki.json, with the source column below each arrow label.\n\n    CA[&#x22;ca.ca_certificate&#x22;]\n    CERT[&#x22;ca.certificate&#x22;]\n    PROFILE[&#x22;ca.issuance_profile&#x22;]\n    DEVICE[&#x22;devicemanager.device&#x22;]\n    DMS[&#x22;dmsmanager.dms&#x22;]\n    KEY[&#x22;kms.kms_key&#x22;]\n    CRL[&#x22;va.crl_settings&#x22;]\n\n    CA -->|&#x22;Issuance profile<br/><code>profile_id</code>&#x22;| PROFILE\n    CA -->|&#x22;Current certificate<br/><code>serial_number</code>&#x22;| CERT\n    CERT -->|&#x22;Issuing CA by ID<br/><code>issuer_meta_id</code>&#x22;| CA\n    CERT -->|&#x22;Issuer serial reference<br/><code>issuer_meta_serial_number</code>&#x22;| CA\n    CERT -->|&#x22;Device by Common Name<br/><code>subject_common_name</code>&#x22;| DEVICE\n    CERT -->|&#x22;Certificate key<br/><code>key_id</code>&#x22;| KEY\n    DEVICE -->|&#x22;Owning DMS<br/><code>dms_owner</code>&#x22;| DMS\n    CRL -->|&#x22;Signer certificate<br/><code>signer_serial_number</code>&#x22;| CERT\n    CRL -->|&#x22;Signer key<br/><code>signer_key_id</code>&#x22;| KEY\"\n/>\n\nA policy can propagate actions from the referenced entity to the one that declares the relationship. For example, to grant read access to a DMS's devices, a rule starts from `dmsmanager.dms`, targets `devicemanager.device` and specifies `via: dms_owner`.\n\nWhen filtering inherited access, `authz` matches the `foreign_key` column against the first `primary_key` column of the referenced entity. For example, it matches `subject_common_name` to `device.id`, `issuer_meta_serial_number` to `ca_certificate.id` and the links to `kms_key` to `kms_key.key_id`.\n\nSchema entities [#schema-entities]\n\n| Entity (`schema_name.entity_type`) | Table (`table_name`) | Key (`primary_key`)   |\n| ---------------------------------- | -------------------- | --------------------- |\n| `alerts.event`                     | `events`             | `event_type`          |\n| `alerts.subscription`              | `subscriptions`      | `id`                  |\n| `ca.ca_certificate`                | `ca_certificates`    | `id`                  |\n| `ca.certificate`                   | `certificates`       | `serial_number`       |\n| `ca.issuance_profile`              | `issuance_profiles`  | `id`                  |\n| `devicemanager.device_group`       | `device_groups`      | `id`                  |\n| `devicemanager.device`             | `devices`            | `id`                  |\n| `dmsmanager.dms`                   | `dms`                | `id`                  |\n| `kms.kms_key`                      | `kms_keys`           | `key_id`, `engine_id` |\n| `va.crl_settings`                  | `crl_settings`       | `ca_id`               |\n\nEvents, subscriptions and device groups have their own actions and filters. Their `relations` lists are empty and they have zero incoming references in the schema. For `ca.certificate`, `view_tables` also lists `certificates_view`.\n\nEach entity declares instance-level operations in `atomic_actions`, operations that require no resource ID in `global_actions`, and the columns and types accepted by `column_filters` in `filterable`.\n\n<Cards>\n  <Card title=\"Access inherited through relations\" href=\"/docs/platform/administration/access-control#access-inherited-through-relations\" />\n</Cards>\n"]
